From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:24:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the DMA controller

The A733 has two DMA controllers with the same register layout. Without
a node for either, nothing on the SoC can use the DMA engine.

Describe DMAC0, the controller Linux uses: 8 KiB at 0x04601000, 16
channels and DRQ ports up to 63, with the bus clock, MBUS clock and reset
of DMA0. The driver takes "dma-requests" as the highest port number.

Not covered: DMAC1 at 0x04024000, which no device needs, and the "dmas"
of the clients.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; sun6i-dma binds DMAC0
at 0x04601000 and dmatest copies through it on 17 channels with 0
failures, its interrupt counting up.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 11776d44e3ac..b68cb5058217 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -611,6 +611,18 @@ mdio0: mdio {
 			};
 		};
 
+		dma: dma-controller@4601000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-dma";
+			reg = <0x04601000 0x2000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 111 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_DMA0>, <&ccu CLK_MBUS_DMA0>;
+			clock-names = "bus", "mbus";
+			dma-channels = <16>;
+			dma-requests = <63>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_DMA0>;
+			#dma-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
 		r_ccu: clock-controller@7010000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-ccu";
 			reg = <0x07010000 0x230>;
